{"name":"Buffalo Herd","hex":"#705046","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"buffalo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An animal from the subtribe Bubalina, also known as true buffalos, such as the Cape buffalo, Syncerus caffer, or the water buffalo, Bubalus bubalis.","A related North American animal, the American bison, Bison bison."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hunt buffalo.","To outwit, confuse, deceive, or intimidate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/buffalo"},{"term":"herd","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A number of domestic animals assembled together under the watch or ownership of a keeper. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Any collection of animals gathered or travelling in a company."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To unite or associate in a herd; to feed or run together, or in company.","To unite or associate in a herd"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/herd"}],"entries":[{"title":"Herd","blocks":[{"text":"A herd is a social group of certain animals of the same species, either wild or domestic. The form of collective animal behavior associated with this is called herding. These animals are known as gregarious animals."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Sheep_and_herder_India.jpg/330px-Sheep_and_herder_India.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herd","wikidata":"Q209542"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Wilderbeest.jpg/500px-Wilderbeest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Wilderbeest.jpg/1280px-Wilderbeest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Wilderbeest.jpg/500px-Wilderbeest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.